//? Title: Bilinear CNNs on actual flower photographs
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Aligned local feature interactions combine two independent VGG-style streams. Hand outer-product and signed-root derivatives,full model execution and actual official-split flower images precede explicit SGD color fitting,visible complete-model Adam and independently restored RGB-only predictions.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/bilinear_cnn.cpp`.

> The method

Average aligned local outer products before smoothed signed-root and unit normalization,then optimize a classifier. Keep the two feature streams independent,fit only the official training subset,and select a checkpoint using separate official validation images.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/bilinear_cnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/bilinear_cnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/bilinear_cnn_concept.tikz > build/bilinear_cnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/bilinear_cnn_concept.svg build/bilinear_cnn_concept.dvi > build/bilinear_cnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
