> Multiply aligned local features before averaging

Two independent encoders see the same observed RGB image. At spatial position
s,they produce feature columns a_s and b_s. Bilinear pooling keeps their local
interactions:

$$M=\frac1S\sum_{s=1}^S a_sb_s^T,\qquad
\frac{\partial L}{\partial a_s}=\frac1S Gb_s,\qquad
\frac{\partial L}{\partial b_s}=\frac1S G^Ta_s.$$
\alttext(The pooled matrix averages aligned local outer products. Its incoming matrix gradient multiplies the opposite feature stream at every location.)

Jointly permuting spatial locations leaves M unchanged. Independently permuting
one stream generally changes it:mean local products are not the outer product
of independently averaged features. For a_0=(1,2),a_1=(3,4),b_0=(2,1),b_1=(0,3),
the mean matrix is[[1,5],[2,7]]. The native independent oracle checks every
matrix entry and both stream Jacobians on signed multi-image features.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bilinear_cnn_outer.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto a = n::tensor({1., 2., 3., 4.}, {1, 1, 2, 2}).requires_grad_(),
       b = n::tensor({2., 1., 0., 3.}, {1, 1, 2, 2}).requires_grad_();
  const auto matrix = n::models::SpatialBilinear(a, b);
  const auto upstream = n::tensor({1., -2., .5, 3.}, {1, 2, 2});
  const auto gradient = n::grad(n::sum(matrix * upstream), {a, b});
  const auto expected = n::tensor({1., 5., 2., 7.}, {1, 2, 2});
  if (n::max(n::abs(matrix - expected)).item() != 0)
    return 1;
  auto left = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(matrix.reshape({2, 2}), {0}), 0, 7),
       right = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(gradient[0].reshape({2, 2}), {0}), -3, 4.5);
  left.title("Mean local outer product");
  left.x_label("stream B channel0,1");
  left.y_label("stream A channel0,1 from bottom");
  right.title("First-stream coordinate derivatives");
  right.x_label("stream A channel0,1");
  right.y_label("spatial position0,1 from bottom");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.add(left).add(right).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/bilinear_cnn_outer.svg");
  std::print("Controlled pooled matrix[[1,5],[2,7]]. Upstream[[1,-2],[.5,3]];first-stream "
             "gradients[[0,2],[-3,4.5]],second-stream[[1,2],[2.5,3]]. No fitting.\n");
}
```
