> Signed square root,then unit normalization

The matrix is flattened,transformed coordinatewise,and normalized:

$$r(x)=\frac{x}{\sqrt{|x|+\epsilon}},\qquad
r'(x)=\frac{.5|x|+\epsilon}{(|x|+\epsilon)^{3/2}},\qquad
u=\frac{r}{\sqrt{\max(r^Tr,10^{-12})}}.$$
\alttext(A smoothed signed square root reduces large bilinear coordinates before squared-norm-floored unit normalization.)

Default epsilon is1e-5;at zero,the signed-root derivative is finite
1/sqrt(epsilon). A completely zero descriptor stays zero. Above the norm floor,
the normalization Jacobian is(I-uu^T)/norm(r);below it,the derivative is
identity/1e-6. The illustration uses epsilon.05 to make the smooth transition
visible;the encoder retains the source1e-5. Native independent derivatives
cover negative,zero,tiny and positive coordinates plus stable extreme-logit CE.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bilinear_cnn_root.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto x = n::linspace(-2, 2, 401).requires_grad_();
  const auto root = n::models::BilinearRoot(x, .05f),
             derivative = n::grad(n::sum(root), {x})[0];
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.lines(x.to_vector<double>(), root.to_vector<double>(), "signed root", {37, 99, 235})
      .title("Smoothed signed square root")
      .x_label("bilinear coordinate")
      .y_label("x / sqrt(abs(x)+.05)")
      .y_limits(-1.6, 1.7);
  b.lines(x.to_vector<double>(), derivative.to_vector<double>(), "derivative", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Finite zero-coordinate derivative")
      .x_label("bilinear coordinate")
      .y_label("d signed root / dx")
      .y_limits(0, 5.3);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg("build/bilinear_cnn_root.svg");
  std::print("Illustrative epsilon.05:zero derivative1/sqrt(.05)={:.6f}. Actual model "
             "epsilon1e-5;native signed-root/unit derivatives include zero and the norm-floor "
             "region.\n",
             1 / std::sqrt(.05));
}
```
