> Both independent VGG-style streams execute

Each stream has13 biased3x3 SAME ReLU convolutions and four2x2/stride2 VALID
max pools. Observed RGB is centred by subtracting.5. The streams have separate
parameter scopes;sharing spatial alignment does not tie their weights. At64px,
the final maps have4x4 spatial positions. Full widths64/128/256/512/512 feed
a512x512 bilinear matrix and102-way head. Compact widths4/8/16/32/32 feed a
32x32 matrix and six-way head. Both variants have54 parameter tensors and37
recorded stages. There is no pretrained state,BN or dropout.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (int divisor : {1, 16}) {
    const int classes = divisor == 1 ? 102 : 6;
    n::ParameterStore p(233);
    auto image =
        (.5 + .4 * n::sin(n::arange(0, 2 * 64 * 64 * 3).reshape({2, 64, 64, 3}) * .13))
            .requires_grad_();
    const auto out = n::models::BilinearCNN(p, image, divisor, classes);
    auto variables = p.parameters();
    variables.push_back(image);
    const auto weights = n::sin(n::arange(0, 2 * classes).reshape({2, classes}) * .17);
    const auto gradients = n::grad(n::sum(out.logits * weights), variables);
    if (p.size() != 54 || out.stages.size() != 37 || gradients.size() != 55)
      return 1;
    for (const auto &g : gradients)
      if (!g.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::norm(g).item()) ||
          (divisor == 16 && n::norm(g).item() <= 0))
        return 1;
    std::print(
        "{} two-stream CNN:{} learned scalars,54 parameter gradients plus RGB gradient;37 "
        "stages;descriptor width{}. Both full and compact actually execute.\n",
        divisor == 1 ? "Full102-way" : "Compact6-way", p.count(), out.descriptor.shape()[1]);
  }
}
```
