> Reproduce the real official-split flower subset

The source expects a prebuilt Flowers archive. This conversion supplies a
preparation command using the original Oxford images,labels and official
split IDs. Download the three files below into a local ignored build cache.
The script verifies the published MD5 values,selects original classes1–6,and
takes the first eight ascending image IDs per class within each official split.
It keeps48 fitting/48 validation/48 test images with144 distinct original IDs.
The report uses local class labels0–5. This explicit selection may differ from
a previously prepared external `flowers.npz`.

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("flowers", (cache / "flowers102").string());
}
```
// result_begin:
// Validated48/48/48 officially disjoint flower images after tensor resizing.
// result_end

Run preparation from the repository root after building the library(or use its
installed pkg-config entry). Python handles only integer metadata and archive
extraction;the adjacent C++ preparation program calls the canonical tensor
image API. Original RGB decoding is byte ingress;division by255 and bilinear
stretching to64x64 are tensor operations. There is no aspect crop,antialias
filter,augmentation,segmentation or bounding-box preprocessing. Source URLs,
checksums,selected IDs and preprocessing are saved in `manifest.json`.
Set `DATAMUNGE_FLOWERS_DIR` to use a prepared directory elsewhere.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bilinear_cnn_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";

  std::filesystem::path root = cache / "flowers102";
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_FLOWERS_DIR"))
    root = p;
  else
    dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("flowers", root.string());

  const auto data = n::models::LoadFlowers(root);
  const std::vector<std::size_t> rows{0, 1, 8, 9, 16, 17, 24, 25, 32, 33, 40, 41};
  const auto preview = n::models::FlowerRows(data.fit, rows);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(preview.rgb, "build/bilinear_cnn_data.png", 2, 0, 1, 3, 1, 3);
  std::print("Real Flowers102 subset:48 fitting/48 validation/48 test images,eight per "
             "selected class,144 unique original IDs. Two actual fitting photos per local "
             "class0–5 shown. IDs/official labels/splits come from checksummed metadata;RGB "
             "preprocessing uses tensor bilinear64px stretch.\n");
}
